# AutoRetainer Integration Rules

## Purpose
Comprehensive guidelines for integrating AutoRetainer plugin functionality into SND macros with proper error handling and best practices.

## Scope
This rule covers AutoRetainer API usage, error handling, character data access, and integration patterns for SND macros.

## AutoRetainer API Integration

### Plugin Availability Check
Always check if AutoRetainer is available before using its functions:

```lua
-- Check if AutoRetainer is available
if IPC.AutoRetainer then
    -- Safe to use AutoRetainer functions
    local isBusy = IPC.AutoRetainer.IsBusy()
else
    yield("/echo [Script] AutoRetainer plugin not available")
    StopFlag = true
end
```

### Basic Status and Control Functions

#### Check Busy State
```lua
-- Check if AutoRetainer is busy
if IPC.AutoRetainer.IsBusy() then
    yield("/echo [Script] AutoRetainer is busy, waiting...")
    while IPC.AutoRetainer.IsBusy() do
        yield("/wait 1")
    end
end
```

#### Multi-Mode Management
```lua
-- Enable multi-mode
IPC.AutoRetainer.EnableMultiMode()

-- Check multi-mode status
local multiModeEnabled = IPC.AutoRetainer.GetMultiModeEnabled()
if not multiModeEnabled then
    IPC.AutoRetainer.SetMultiModeEnabled(true)
end
```

### Character Data Access (Critical)

#### Safe Character Data Retrieval
**CRITICAL**: Always use `Svc.ClientState.LocalContentId` instead of `Player.CID` to avoid SEHException:

```lua
-- ✅ CORRECT - Use Svc.ClientState.LocalContentId
local currentCharId = Svc.ClientState.LocalContentId
local characterData = IPC.AutoRetainer.GetOfflineCharacterData(currentCharId)

-- ❌ WRONG - Causes SEHException
-- local characterData = IPC.AutoRetainer.GetOfflineCharacterData(Player.CID)
```

#### Safe Character Data Function
```lua
function GetCharacterDataSafely(charId)
    if not charId then
        yield("/echo [Script] Error: No character ID provided")
        return nil
    end
    
    local success, data = pcall(function()
        return IPC.AutoRetainer.GetOfflineCharacterData(charId)
    end)
    
    if success and data then
        return data
    else
        yield("/echo [Script] Error: Could not retrieve character data for ID " .. tostring(charId))
        return nil
    end
end

-- Usage
local safeCharData = GetCharacterDataSafely(Svc.ClientState.LocalContentId)
if safeCharData and safeCharData.RetainersAwaitingProcessing then
    yield("/echo [Script] Retainers are waiting to be processed")
end
```

### Inventory Management

#### Check Inventory Space
```lua
-- Check free inventory slots
local freeSlots = IPC.AutoRetainer.GetInventoryFreeSlotCount()
if freeSlots < 5 then
    yield("/echo [Script] Warning: Low inventory space (" .. freeSlots .. " slots)")
    -- Handle low inventory space
else
    yield("/echo [Script] Inventory space OK (" .. freeSlots .. " slots)")
end
```

#### Retainer Availability Check
```lua
-- Check if retainers are available
if IPC.AutoRetainer.AreAnyRetainersAvailableForCurrentChara() then
    yield("/echo [Script] Retainers are available for current character")
    -- Proceed with retainer operations
else
    yield("/echo [Script] No retainers available for current character")
end
```

### Task Management

#### Enqueue Operations
```lua
-- Enqueue initiation task
IPC.AutoRetainer.EnqueueInitiation()
yield("/echo [Script] Initiation task enqueued")

-- Enqueue HET task with retry on failure
IPC.AutoRetainer.EnqueueHET(true)  -- true = retry on failure
```

#### Abort Operations
```lua
-- Abort all tasks
IPC.AutoRetainer.AbortAllTasks()
yield("/echo [Script] All AutoRetainer tasks aborted")

-- Disable all functions
IPC.AutoRetainer.DisableAllFunctions()
yield("/echo [Script] All AutoRetainer functions disabled")
```

