## Complete AutoRetainer Workflow Pattern

### Standard Workflow Function
```lua
function HandleAutoRetainerWorkflow()
    -- Check if AutoRetainer is available
    if not IPC.AutoRetainer or IPC.AutoRetainer.IsBusy() then
        yield("/echo [Script] AutoRetainer not available")
        return false
    end
    
    -- Check inventory space
    local freeSlots = IPC.AutoRetainer.GetInventoryFreeSlotCount()
    if freeSlots < 3 then
        yield("/echo [Script] Not enough inventory space")
        return false
    end
    
    -- Check if retainers need processing
    local charData = GetCharacterDataSafely(Svc.ClientState.LocalContentId)
    if charData and charData.RetainersAwaitingProcessing then
        yield("/echo [Script] Enabling AutoRetainer for retainer processing")
        IPC.AutoRetainer.EnableMultiMode()
        return true
    else
        yield("/echo [Script] No retainers need processing")
        return false
    end
end
```

### State Machine Integration
```lua
-- Add AutoRetainer state to your state machine
CharacterState = {
    ready = Ready,
    processRetainers = ProcessRetainers,
    -- ... other states
}

function ProcessRetainers()
    if HandleAutoRetainerWorkflow() then
        -- Wait for AutoRetainer to complete
        while IPC.AutoRetainer.IsBusy() do
            yield("/wait 1")
        end
        yield("/echo [Script] AutoRetainer processing completed")
    end
    State = CharacterState.ready
end
```

## Error Handling Patterns

### Common Error Solutions

#### SEHException Prevention
```lua
-- Always use Svc.ClientState.LocalContentId
local charId = Svc.ClientState.LocalContentId
local charData = IPC.AutoRetainer.GetOfflineCharacterData(charId)
```

#### API Availability Check
```lua
-- Check if AutoRetainer is available
if not IPC.AutoRetainer then
    yield("/echo [Script] ERROR: AutoRetainer plugin not available")
    StopFlag = true
    return
end
```

#### Safe Function Calls
```lua
-- Use pcall for potentially failing operations
local success, result = pcall(function()
    return IPC.AutoRetainer.SomeFunction()
end)

if not success then
    yield("/echo [Script] ERROR: AutoRetainer function failed: " .. tostring(result))
    return nil
end
```

## Best Practices

### 1. Always Check API Availability
```lua
if not IPC.AutoRetainer then
    yield("/echo [Script] AutoRetainer not available")
    return
end
```

### 2. Use Proper Character ID
```lua
-- Always use Svc.ClientState.LocalContentId
local charId = Svc.ClientState.LocalContentId
```

### 3. Implement Error Handling
```lua
-- Use pcall for all AutoRetainer operations
local success, data = pcall(function()
    return IPC.AutoRetainer.GetOfflineCharacterData(charId)
end)
```

### 4. Check Inventory Space
```lua
-- Always check inventory before starting tasks
local freeSlots = IPC.AutoRetainer.GetInventoryFreeSlotCount()
if freeSlots < 3 then
    yield("/echo [Script] Not enough inventory space")
    return
end
```

### 5. Handle Busy States
```lua
-- Wait for AutoRetainer to finish
while IPC.AutoRetainer.IsBusy() do
    yield("/wait 1")
end
```

### 6. Use Multi-Mode Appropriately
```lua
-- Enable multi-mode when needed
if charData and charData.RetainersAwaitingProcessing then
    IPC.AutoRetainer.EnableMultiMode()
end
```

## Configuration Integration

### AutoRetainer Configuration Variables
```lua
-- Add to your macro's configs section
configs:
  EnableAutoRetainer:
    default: true
    description: Enable AutoRetainer integration
  MinInventorySlots:
    default: 5
    description: Minimum free inventory slots required
  AutoRetainerTimeout:
    default: 300
    description: AutoRetainer operation timeout in seconds
```

### Usage in Code
```lua
-- Get configuration values
local enableAutoRetainer = Config.Get("EnableAutoRetainer") == "true"
local minInventorySlots = tonumber(Config.Get("MinInventorySlots"))
local timeout = tonumber(Config.Get("AutoRetainerTimeout"))

-- Use in logic
if enableAutoRetainer and IPC.AutoRetainer then
    local freeSlots = IPC.AutoRetainer.GetInventoryFreeSlotCount()
    if freeSlots >= minInventorySlots then
        -- Proceed with AutoRetainer operations
    end
end
```

